# Generating a generic POM

Sometimes you do not have a POM for a third-party artifact. This happens, for example, when you install a proprietary or commercial JAR. The Install Plugin can create a generic POM for such an artifact. The generic POM contains the minimal set of POM elements that Maven requires, such as groupId, artifactId, version, and packaging.

Set the `generatePom` parameter to `true`. Maven will then generate the POM.

```unknown
mvn ${project.groupId}:${project.artifactId}:${project.version}:install-file  -Dfile=path-to-your-artifact-jar \
                                                                              -DgroupId=your.groupId \
                                                                              -DartifactId=your-artifactId \
                                                                              -Dversion=version \
                                                                              -Dpackaging=jar \
                                                                              -DgeneratePom=true
```

**Note**: Use the fully qualified path of a goal. This ensures that you use the preferred version of the maven-install-plugin. When you use `mvn install:install-file`, the plugin version depends on the POM or the Apache Maven version.
